# Line endings are content as far as a digest is concerned.
#
# The public red-team challenge is verified by hashing the files a challenger
# checks out. Git converts line endings on checkout, so without a policy here a
# clone under core.autocrlf=true produces different bytes than the tree the
# freeze was computed in -- which is exactly the defect published as w3-e2.1.
#
# This is defence in depth, not the fix. The freeze canonicalizes CRLF to LF
# before hashing, so verification holds even for a checkout that ignores this
# file. Both together mean a challenger sees the same digest either way.
redteam/**      text eol=lf

# The frozen challenge record must never be rewritten by a checkout filter.
redteam/FREEZE.json   text eol=lf
